==English==

===Etymology===
{{unk.|en}} etymology, 1813.<ref>{{R:Merriam Webster Online}}</ref> Original sense “alcoholic drink”, possibly a variant of {{m|en|switchel||a drink of molasses and water, often mixed with rum}}, attested 1790, itself of uncertain origin.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> Possibly influenced by {{m|en|fizz}}.

In verb sense “to stir”, from {{m|en|swizzle stick||stick for stirring alcoholic drinks}}, itself attested 1859.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪzəl|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various kinds of [[alcoholic]] [[drink]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|swizzle stick}}

====See also====
* {{l|en|cocktail}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|swizzl}}

# To [[stir]] or [[mix]].
#: ''She '''swizzled''' the milk into her coffee.''
# {{label|en|computing}} To [[permute]] [[bits]].
# {{label|en|computing|programming|transitive}} To [[convert]] [[portable]] [[symbol]]s or [[position]]s to [[memory]]-dependent [[pointer]]s during [[deserialization]].
# To drink; to swill.
#: {{rfquotek|Halliwell}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|convert symbols to pointers}} {{l|en|unswizzle}}

